{#
  The period on the address could not be read, so no figure is drawn: showing another
  period's numbers under the one that was asked for would be worse than showing none.

  The bar at the top still offers the periods that can be read, so the page is a way
  out and not a dead end.

  Expected: view.refused, plus the shell's own.
#}{% extends "layout.njk" %}

{% block title %}period — webtools metrics{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<section class="failure">
  <h2>The period on the address could not be read</h2>
  <table class="grid">
    <tbody>
      <tr><th>from</th><td>{% if view.refused.from !== null %}<code>{{ view.refused.from }}</code>{% else %}<span class="absent">not on the address</span>{% endif %}</td></tr>
      <tr><th>to</th><td>{% if view.refused.to !== null %}<code>{{ view.refused.to }}</code>{% else %}<span class="absent">not on the address</span>{% endif %}</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>A period is <strong>two</strong> days, both written <code>YYYY-MM-DD</code> and in UTC, the first no later
    than the second. Today is {{ view.refused.today }}.</p>
  <p>Nothing was read. The bar at the top will read a period that can be read.</p>
</section>
{% endblock %}
